  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 334511) has $11.5B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The federal market recorded 7,052 awards in the same period, with an average award size of $1.6M. Obligations are down 37.2% year over year, after peaking at $18.4B in FY25 and falling to $11.5B in FY26 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $9.5B, followed by the Department of Transportation at $1B and the Department of Homeland Security at $842M. Top vendors include RAYTHEON COMPANY with multiple award totals including $1.6B and $580M entries, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION with $855M and $302M entries. Fiscal-year comparisons show FY21 at $13.2B, FY22 at $13.9B, FY23 at $17B, FY24 at $17.1B, FY25 at $18.4B, and FY26 at $11.5B. Current-year totals are partial because figures reflect fiscal year to date contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
